WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.077
The FBA Inventory page in Seller Central consolidates information about your FBA inventory in one

00:00:08.077 --> 00:00:14.000
place to help you maintain your inventory performance metrics and health.

00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:21.391
Unlike the Manage All Inventory page, which shows all your ASINs, FBA inventory will only show ASINs

00:00:21.391 --> 00:00:24.000
that you have enrolled in FBA.

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:28.000
If you haven't enrolled any ASINs yet, this page may be blank.

00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:36.100
To get to the FBA Inventory page in Seller Central, open the menu, hover over Inventory, and click

00:00:36.100 --> 00:00:37.000
FBA Inventory.

00:00:37.000 --> 00:00:42.909
Your dashboard has multiple columns which show metrics, including fee estimates, inventory health,

00:00:42.909 --> 00:00:47.000
sell-through rates, and recommended actions for each SKU.

00:00:47.000 --> 00:00:53.000
Hover over the information icon in each column for a detailed description of each metric.

00:00:53.000 --> 00:00:59.750
You can also choose filters to group products with similar inventory characteristics, such as age,

00:00:59.750 --> 00:01:02.000
storage type, and product condition.

00:01:02.000 --> 00:01:07.000
These filters can make it easier to decide what recommended actions to take.

00:01:07.000 --> 00:01:13.154
By using the search feature, you can find items that have similar product characteristics such as

00:01:13.154 --> 00:01:17.000
SKU, ASIN, or any product details like color or quantity.

00:01:17.000 --> 00:01:21.125
You can then sort, filter, and action these items.

00:01:21.125 --> 00:01:28.000
We encourage you to regularly monitor your FBA Inventory page to maintain healthy inventory levels.
